{"id":5901,"date":"2022-03-02T13:39:01","date_gmt":"2022-03-02T21:39:01","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=5901"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:37:12","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:37:12","slug":"3-2-battery-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/3-2-battery-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"3.2: Battery"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dc771\" name=\"6a221370dc771\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761251830868{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dc925\" name=\"6a221370dc925\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Goals and Steps to Success<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Goals:<\/p>\n<p>By the end of this lesson, I will be able to:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Explain the importance of measuring battery level<\/li>\n<li>Describe how the battery level is reported by your CoDrone EDU<\/li>\n<li>Use the get_battery_percentage function to measure the drone&#8217;s battery level<\/li>\n<li>Store and print the drone&#8217;s battery level<\/li>\n<li>Use battery level to restrict flight movements<\/li>\n<li>Use the LED to indicate battery level<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Steps to Success:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Battery Indicator<\/li>\n<li>Printing the Battery Level<\/li>\n<li>Before and After<\/li>\n<li>Limiting Takeoff<\/li>\n<li>Adding the LED<\/li>\n<li>Add Conditionals to Your LED Program<\/li>\n<li>Adding elif Statements<\/li>\n<li>Adding an else Statement<\/li>\n<li>Final LED Code<\/li>\n<li>Challenge 1: Battery Calculator<\/li>\n<li>Challenge 2: Battery Charge Reporter<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dc9ad\" name=\"6a221370dc9ad\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Battery Indicator<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Most electronic devices use batteries. Your laptop, cellphone, radio, TV remote, video game consoles, and even your car all have batteries.<em> How do you know when your device needs to be charged or replaced?<\/em><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7746&#8243; img_size=&#8221;546&#215;462&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Typically, a red battery icon or LED will let you know that a battery is running low. You may have noticed your CoDrone EDU flashing red and making a sound when the battery is running low. In this lesson, you will learn how to request the battery level and change the LED yourself!<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dca1e\" name=\"6a221370dca1e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Printing the Battery Level<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Requesting the battery level may not seem like a sensor reading, but you are actually measuring the battery&#8217;s <strong>voltage<\/strong>. Open the senior &#8220;Sensors&#8221; category to find the <strong>get_battery<\/strong> block near the middle of the list.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;6078&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dca89\" name=\"6a221370dca89\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Before and After<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>You probably won\u2019t notice a big difference in the percentage yet, so add some flying! Print the battery percentage before and after hovering for 10 seconds.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;6079&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div><em>What was the difference?<\/em> You might notice that it drops a lot! This is because you are actually reading the voltage value at that moment in time. After your program ends, you will notice that the battery level comes back up after a few seconds.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dcafa\" name=\"6a221370dcafa\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Limiting Takeoff<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>In this exercise, you will write a program that will either take off or do nothing, depending on the battery level.<\/div>\n<div>First, include the program that you wrote in the last step, which will print out your drone\u2019s battery level. Next, write a conditional so that if the battery level is greater than 50, it will take off, hover for 2 seconds, and land. Else, it will print \u201cNot enough power!\u201d and stay grounded.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12911&#8243; img_size=&#8221;400&#215;565&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Try changing the battery level in the conditional to a different number. <em>What happens?<\/em><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dcb59\" name=\"6a221370dcb59\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Adding the LED<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>The LED on your CoDrone EDU already acts as a battery indicator \u2014 when your battery is low, it flashes red. In this program, you will be adding more colors to indicate different battery percentages.<\/div>\n<div>First, start with the code from the last step that will print the battery percentage.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12913&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dcbcf\" name=\"6a221370dcbcf\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Add Conditionals to Your LED Program<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You are going to use conditionals to check your battery\u2019s percentage. Depending on your battery level, your CoDrone EDU&#8217;s LED will turn a certain color. You can change them to whatever you want, but we recommend you make them easy to tell apart so you know when you need to charge your battery. This is what we&#8217;re going to use for this lesson:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">100-76: solid green LED<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">75-51: solid yellow LED<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">50-26: solid red LED<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">25-0: will not fly<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Next, write an if statement that will change your CoDrone EDU\u2019s LED to green when the battery level is above 75%. Include a delay, so flight movements after the LED change aren\u2019t skipped, and then add a takeoff command.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12914&#8243; img_size=&#8221;400&#215;243&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dcc35\" name=\"6a221370dcc35\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Adding Else If Statements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Do the same for 51-75% battery and then 26-50% battery, but with a few changes:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instead of if statements, use else if statements.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instead of the battery being greater than 75%, it should be greater than 50% and then 25%.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12915&#8243; img_size=&#8221;450&#215;759&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dcc8c\" name=\"6a221370dcc8c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Adding an Else Statement<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Add an else statement to indicate that if none of the above statements are true and your battery is less than 25%, your drone does not have enough power to fly!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;6084&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">All the conditionals above 25% have a takeoff command included, so include any flight commands you would like in your program after the else statement. <em>Don\u2019t forget to land and close your drone!<\/em><\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dccda\" name=\"6a221370dccda\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 11<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final LED Code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your final code should look like this:<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12916&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dcd46\" name=\"6a221370dcd46\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 12<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge 1: Battery Calculator<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]For this challenge, we want to predict whether our drone will be able to fly the flight path we have programmed for it. To do this, repeat the step where we checked the difference in battery power after a takeoff, wait, and land. Figure out how much battery is lost per 5 seconds of flight time:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Takeoff, hover 5 seconds, land -&gt; take before and after battery measurements<\/li>\n<li>Takeoff, hover 10 seconds, land -&gt; take before and after battery measurements<\/li>\n<li>Take the difference of the battery usage between steps 1 and 2. This is your battery drain per 5 seconds of stationary flight.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>Now, write a flight plan that has at least 5 movements and at least 30 seconds of flight time. Store the beginning and ending battery percentage. Also store the beginning and ending flight time. Print both of these values at the end of the flight, after landing.<\/p>\n<p>When you run the program, time it and make a prediction as to how much battery life you will lose. Check your drone&#8217;s output versus your prediction<em>. How close was your prediction? What could be causing any differences?<\/em>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221370dcd92\" name=\"6a221370dcd92\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 13<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In this lesson, you learned about the CoDrone EDU&#8217;s battery sensor, including how to access and print the data from the sensor! You can use this battery sensor data for a variety of things, such as limiting takeoff or forcing the CoDrone EDU to land depending on the battery level.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 14 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761251830868{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved 